  "result": "Excellent! All 136 tests pass \u2713\n\n**Summary of additions:**\n\n1. **src/customers.js** \u2014 Exported customer tier discount mapping:\n   ```javascript\n   export const TIER_DISCOUNTS = {\n     gold: 5,\n     silver: 2.5,\n     standard: 0,\n   };\n   ```\n\n2. **src/invoices.js** \u2014 Updated to apply tier discounts:\n   - `createInvoice()` \u2014 When a line lacks explicit `discountPercent`, applies the customer's tier discount\n   - `addLine()` \u2014 When adding a new line without `discountPercent`, applies the customer's tier discount\n   - Lines with explicit `discountPercent` (even 0) always win over tier discount\n\n3. **Discount logic:**\n   - If `line.discountPercent` is defined (even if 0), use that\n   - If undefined, use `TIER_DISCOUNTS[customer.tier]`\n   - Standard tier (0%) means no discount field added unless explicitly provided\n   - Tier percentages centralized in one place for easy maintenance\n\n4. **Test coverage** \u2014 11 new tests covering:\n   - Gold, silver, standard tier discounts (5%, 2.5%, 0%)\n   - Explicit discount overriding tier discount\n   - Zero discount explicitly overriding tier discount\n   - Multiple lines with tier discounts\n   - Mixed explicit and tier discounts\n   - addLine applying tier discounts\n   - Invoice totals with tier discounts\n\n5. **Updated 6 existing tests** to account for the new tier discount behavior\n\nThe implementation ensures that every customer automatically receives their tier discount unless explicitly overridden on a per-line basis.",
